Q: switching between forward and reverse iteration A: <p>Here is one way to do it using templates:</p>

<pre><code>template&lt;typename It&gt;
void foo(It begin, It end) {
  for (It it = begin; it != end; ++it) {
    // ...
  }
}

void bar(std::vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; m_levels, bool reverse) {
  if (reverse) {
    foo(m_levels.rbegin(), m_levels.rend());
  } else {
    foo(m_levels.begin(), m_levels.end());
  }
}
</code></pre>

<p>The idea is to move the logic into a helper function that's parameterized by the iterator type. It can then be called with either forward or reverse iterators.</p>
